    "durationMs": 174055,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Here's what I built and confirmed:\n\n**Project structure**\n- `app/main.py` — FastAPI app with all four endpoints and exception handlers so every 4xx response carries an `error` field (including malformed-JSON 422s)\n- `app/schemas.py` — validation: absolute http/https URL with a host, code matching `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`; submitted URLs are stored and returned byte-for-byte unchanged\n- `app/models.py` + `alembic/versions/0001` — SQLAlchemy `links` table with unique code and a server-side default for clicks, applied via Alembic\n- `app/config.py` — reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (no hard-coded credentials), rewires it to the psycopg3 driver\n- `start.sh` — runs `python3 -m alembic upgrade head`, then `exec`s uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; dependencies are not installed there\n- `README.md` — quick-start section; `requirements.txt` pins the preinstalled versions; `tests/test_api.py` ships 21 tests\n\n**Verified against the live server**\n- POST returns 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}`; generated codes are unique 8-char strings; duplicate custom codes → 409 with `error`\n- Invalid/missing URLs (relative, ftp, empty host, wrong types), invalid codes (too short/long, bad charset), and malformed JSON all → 422 with `error`\n- GET `/links/{code}` and unknown codes → correct 200/404 shapes; `/r/{code}` → 302 with exact `Location` and clicks incremented exactly once per hit (atomic SQL `clicks + 1`)\n- GET `/links` returns ascending creation order with matching `total`\n- Full restart test: killed the server, re-ran `sh start.sh` — all links and click counts survived, migrations applied idempotently\n\nAll 21 pytest tests pass, and the server was stopped cleanly so port 8000 is free for the automated suite."
